TO DO for Rtl66 0.2
Chris Ahlstrom
2019-04-13 to 2025-12-09

For version 0.3:

    -   Get one of the Windows APIs to work.
    -   Add a test app to record one track, write it to a
        file, read the file, and play it.

Fixes:

    -   Why is the note off always at time 0?

        [cbmidiin] Msg:  3 bytes @ 3285302:  0x90 0x41 0x43 buss/index 255
        [cbmidiin] Msg:  3 bytes @ 0:  0x80 0x41 0x40 buss/index 255

    -   Track down the "uninitialized semaphores" in JACK.
    -   Why does JACK detection when JACK is not running take
        so long?
    -   The midiprobeex does not fall back to ALSA, it just fails.
    -   Fix busin functionality and get_message(). DONE.
        -   The event type includes codes for note on/off and other
            specific events; we should take advantage of this.
    -   Make sure meaningful JACK device aliases can be found.
    -   A sporadic race condition in JACK playback.
    -   play does not reload the PPQN (and BPM?) for each file.
    -   midiprobeex doubles the number of ports.
    -   In create_track(), use the initial track number as a parameter.
    -   In event::append_meta_data(), the message is actually cleared
        before appending. Rename the function or add a bool 'clear' flag.
    -   Make sure trackdata::parse() sets track number correctly.
    -   Update rterror to print the client-tag in error messages.
    -   Investigate differences between behavior of cbmidiin and qmidiin.
    -   In cfg, how about a convention where, instead of just

            --callback      -c

        we have stuff like

            --&callback     which provides -c
            --call&back     which provides -b
            --&call&back    which provides -cb

